---
title: Stir-fried Vegetables with Tofu
servings: 3
course: dinner
tags: vegetarian, vegan
source: https://www.marmiton.org/recettes/recette_legumes-sautes-au-tofu_15314.aspx
time: 25m
---

Saute the @onion{1}, @sesame seed{1%tbsp}, @garlic powder{0.5%tsp}, @ground coriander{0.5%tsp} and @cumin{0.5%tsp} in @soy sauce{3%tbsp} in a #pan{} (except the chili which you will add at the end of cooking).

Add the @tofu{1%block} cut into small cubes. When the tofu is seared, add the @red bell pepper{2} and @green bell pepper{1} cut into diamonds or strips. Then add the @tomato{2} roughly crushed.

Stir often, add the @sugar{1%tsp} and add more spices during cooking if you wish.

Continue cooking for ~{3%minutes} after adding the @chili powder{}.

Remove from heat and mix in the @bean sprout{1%handful} and @fresh coriander{}.

Drizzle with @sesame oil{}.

Once you have mastered this base you can add, to taste, mushrooms, carrots, broccoli or sliced cabbage.
